    "findings": [
      "Selection isolates the intended cross and star instead of multiple baskets or the neighboring heart. The automatic star-scene success is the wrong basket and is excluded from intended-object success.",
      "Pale printed checker has a complete silhouette with either SAM box; supplied selection suppresses the handle. Both yield checked 2/2-cut checker masks, but uneven cell boundaries and point-contact uncertainty remain.",
      "Pale-checker right/left corners lie inside approximate visible ranges; both tips overshoot the range and lie slightly outside the photograph. Unknown notch is unscored. Partial observation coverage remains active.",
      "Cross retains a false small central diamond. Star retains rounded joins and thin seams.",
      "Dense checker crop is plausible but its current low-count fitting loses cells. The separate expanded-count experiment uses the earlier RGB crop/target and is not merged into these results.",
      "Automatic gold-tree crop includes extra paper/background; material field and weave lose the intended tree. Selected box does not produce a supported crop.",
      "Painted heart remains a segmentation failure in both arms.",
      "Red/green printed source gets a selected crop but fails BEFORE fitting: inverse letterbox width 3729.9999999999995 versus 3730 is rejected as incomplete prediction coverage. Numerical repair and replay are pending; this is not a solver timeout."
    ]
  },
